1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:11,800
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,633 --> 00:00:32,900
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,333
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,667 --> 00:00:41,833
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:43,333 --> 00:00:44,033
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,400
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:46,267
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,267
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:54,033
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,167 --> 00:00:55,667
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,733 --> 00:00:57,633
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,200
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,033 --> 00:01:02,700
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,067 --> 00:01:06,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:11,567
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:12,167
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:21,133
<i>So where's the medicine
you bought?</i>

21
00:01:21,133 --> 00:01:22,700
<i>I passed by a group
of men playing cards. I lost.</i>

22
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:25,133
<i>You know, Rudy,
Gabo worked hard to earn it.</i>

23
00:01:25,133 --> 00:01:26,633
<i>- Who's dirty?
- You're the dirty one!</i>

24
00:01:26,633 --> 00:01:28,400
<i>Now, quit acting
like you're all clean!</i>

25
00:01:28,533 --> 00:01:31,433
Because we're all dirty, anyway!

26
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:32,567
<i> Betchay!</i>

27
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:33,767
<i>Where did Gabo get
that huge sum of money from?</i>

28
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,067
<i> Even if you kill us,
</i>you won't get anything from us.

29
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,167
<i>- Kill them.
- No! Stop!</i>

30
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:39,300
<i> We can spy on Gabo for you.</i>

31
00:01:39,467 --> 00:01:41,233
- [GUNSHOTS]
<i> - I don't want to die!</i>

32
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,800
<i>The moment I find out
your parents were involved,</i>

33
00:01:43,933 --> 00:01:45,267
<i>all of you are going
to rot in prison.</i>

34
00:01:45,367 --> 00:01:47,100
<i>Why don't you arrest
the long-haired guy?</i>

35
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:48,167
<i> You know that guy?</i>

36
00:01:48,167 --> 00:01:50,033
<i>That's for me to know,
and for you to find out.</i>

37
00:01:50,033 --> 00:01:52,533
<i>That's why we need
your help, Gabo.</i>

38
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:55,067
<i>As long as our nation
remains in poverty...</i>

39
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:56,933
<i>We need to cleanse
our society</i>

40
00:01:57,067 --> 00:01:58,700
and fix the entire Philippines.

41
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:00,400
<i>We will give you
everything you need.</i>

42
00:02:00,467 --> 00:02:02,700
You need to operate undetected.

43
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:11,667
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,533
No one will recognize you now.

45
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:21,200
Pops, do I really need
to dress like this?

46
00:02:21,333 --> 00:02:24,733
There are times
when you need to blend in

47
00:02:24,867 --> 00:02:26,733
for the sake of your missions.

48
00:02:26,867 --> 00:02:28,700
You need to be all suited up.

49
00:02:29,467 --> 00:02:33,000
On top of that, that suit
is really special, Gabo.

50
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,733
It's made out of bulletproof

51
00:02:36,733 --> 00:02:38,467
and fireproof materials.

52
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,800
We had it made in Europe.

53
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:44,600
It's made out of
a dragon scale fabric.

54
00:02:45,467 --> 00:02:48,167
It's as strong
as a dragon's skin.

55
00:02:48,933 --> 00:02:51,267
And it'll protect you too.

56
00:02:53,733 --> 00:02:54,800
That means...

57
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:59,533
I'd be protected
from fire and bullets

58
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:00,633
when I'm wearing this.

59
00:03:00,767 --> 00:03:04,800
People who will attack
you from the front

60
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:06,200
won't be able to hurt you.

61
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,400
Gabo.

62
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:09,433
Come with me.

63
00:03:09,433 --> 00:03:11,733
We're going to show you the guns
you'll be using.

64
00:03:12,667 --> 00:03:13,667
Please.

65
00:03:17,367 --> 00:03:21,333
- [FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

66
00:03:22,533 --> 00:03:23,300
[ROSANNA] Ibyang!

67
00:03:23,433 --> 00:03:24,967
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS]

68
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:26,533
- [IBYANG] Why?
- Come here!

69
00:03:26,667 --> 00:03:27,733
Come take a look at this.

70
00:03:28,633 --> 00:03:31,000
- What is it?
- We need to order more beer.

71
00:03:31,133 --> 00:03:32,700
We need to get more of these.

72
00:03:33,767 --> 00:03:35,067
We're running low?

73
00:03:35,967 --> 00:03:38,333
A lot of our customers
have been ordering beer.

74
00:03:38,467 --> 00:03:39,300
It's because of Betchay.

75
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:42,267
We sold a lot last night.
We were packed.

76
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,200
- [CHUCKLES]
- Yeah, we did.

77
00:03:44,333 --> 00:03:45,900
But all the bottles were broken.

78
00:03:46,033 --> 00:03:47,733
That's still a loss!

79
00:03:47,867 --> 00:03:48,600
True that.

80
00:03:48,733 --> 00:03:50,333
She's a complete mess
when drunk.

81
00:03:50,467 --> 00:03:52,033
Oh please, give Betchay a break.

82
00:03:52,167 --> 00:03:53,800
Oh, come on.

83
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:56,267
Did Betchay even pay
for the broken bottles?

84
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,067
I already included it
on her tab, Ibyang.

85
00:03:58,200 --> 00:03:59,700
We'll deduct it
from her paycheck.

86
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:00,300
As it should.

87
00:04:00,433 --> 00:04:05,967
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

88
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:06,933
[MUSIC FADES]

89
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:08,167
- Mameng.
- Hmm?

90
00:04:08,233 --> 00:04:10,433
- Where's Rudy?
- He's in there--

91
00:04:10,567 --> 00:04:11,533
Oh, there he is.

92
00:04:12,167 --> 00:04:13,067
Dy...

93
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:15,667
Where have you been?

94
00:04:15,667 --> 00:04:17,800
Oh, I needed some fresh air.

95
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:18,833
Uh, Dy,

96
00:04:19,667 --> 00:04:24,533
there are people from NGO
who want to help us.

97
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,767
They're the ones
who came here last time.

98
00:04:26,767 --> 00:04:30,133
I used the money
to pay for the hospital bills.

99
00:04:30,167 --> 00:04:33,367
The people who Gabo threw out?

100
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:35,567
- Yes, that's them.
- [PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

101
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:37,233
I don't get your son.

102
00:04:38,133 --> 00:04:41,300
They're offering help
and we're refusing to let them.

103
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:43,600
Hold on.

104
00:04:43,733 --> 00:04:45,600
What do they really want anyway?

105
00:04:45,733 --> 00:04:47,033
Gabo is suspicious of them.

106
00:04:47,167 --> 00:04:48,400
I think they're just cops.

107
00:04:48,533 --> 00:04:49,733
And so what if they're cops?

108
00:04:49,867 --> 00:04:51,000
They're willing to help.

109
00:04:52,833 --> 00:04:54,000
They're easy to talk to.

110
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:57,433
And Rudy,

111
00:04:57,567 --> 00:05:01,200
that'll help us recover
from all the hospital bills.

112
00:05:01,367 --> 00:05:05,833
Instead of taking the case
to court.

113
00:05:05,967 --> 00:05:08,033
We won't get anything
out of that.

114
00:05:08,167 --> 00:05:09,567
Oh, let me stop you right there.

115
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,267
"Get nothing out of it?"

116
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:14,300
Rudy is seeking justice,
not money.

117
00:05:14,433 --> 00:05:15,500
Justice?

118
00:05:16,467 --> 00:05:18,733
[SCOFFS]
We're fighting against cops.

119
00:05:18,867 --> 00:05:21,033
Did you forget that?

120
00:05:21,167 --> 00:05:22,300
They implement the law.

121
00:05:22,433 --> 00:05:24,067
And you want us
to file a case against them?

122
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:27,600
Tell me,
can you pay for a lawyer?

123
00:05:27,733 --> 00:05:28,700
- Gabo can--
- Gabo again.

124
00:05:28,833 --> 00:05:32,267
It's always Gabo! Gabo!

125
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,933
You don't even ask him where
he gets the money he gives us!

126
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:38,367
And you can't be sure
if it'll keep coming!

127
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:40,233
And those people
are offering it now!

128
00:05:41,367 --> 00:05:42,833
They'll put it
right on our hands!

129
00:05:43,767 --> 00:05:47,433
Hold on.
Can we talk about this calmly?

130
00:05:47,433 --> 00:05:49,967
Rudy, come on,
we've talked about this.

131
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:53,267
You know
the justice you're seeking

132
00:05:53,267 --> 00:05:54,967
is only for the rich.

133
00:05:57,933 --> 00:05:59,167
[RUDY SIGHS]

134
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:01,333
Rudy.

135
00:06:01,467 --> 00:06:04,533
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

136
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,433
[MUSIC FADES]

137
00:06:06,567 --> 00:06:07,700
Ma'am.

138
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:10,533
- Ma'am Pinky is here.
- [ISOBEL] Oh.

139
00:06:10,533 --> 00:06:12,367
- Hi, Isobel.
- Hi, my dear Pinky.

140
00:06:12,367 --> 00:06:13,600
I brought you something.

141
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:15,267
Thank you. Thank you.

142
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:17,433
Have a seat.

143
00:06:17,433 --> 00:06:20,033
I just want to know
how you're doing,

144
00:06:20,167 --> 00:06:21,533
and the whole family as well

145
00:06:21,667 --> 00:06:24,700
after what happened last night.

146
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:25,900
Pinky, I'm sorry

147
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:28,633
you had to witness
Ricardo making a scene

148
00:06:28,633 --> 00:06:30,167
in front of the guests.

149
00:06:30,433 --> 00:06:33,100
You don't have
to apologize to me.

150
00:06:33,233 --> 00:06:34,933
How was Sam
after what happened last night?

151
00:06:35,833 --> 00:06:39,567
She's still trying to be okay
ever since RJ died.

152
00:06:39,567 --> 00:06:42,800
Even though her Dad
treats her that way,

153
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:46,467
I'm trying to make up for
Ricardo's shortcomings.

154
00:06:46,467 --> 00:06:48,767
But I know
it's still not enough.

155
00:06:48,767 --> 00:06:53,767
Sam is paying for something
that wasn't even her fault.

156
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:55,967
You know, Pinky
this is my family.

157
00:06:55,967 --> 00:06:59,433
Far from the family
I've dreamed of.

158
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:02,300
I don't know
if we'll ever be okay.

159
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,867
Isobel, don't lose hope.

160
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,833
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:07:08,967 --> 00:07:10,133
Thank you.

162
00:07:23,133 --> 00:07:30,133
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

163
00:07:34,967 --> 00:07:38,367
[PHONE RINGING]

164
00:07:41,567 --> 00:07:43,467
- Max?
<i> - Sam.</i>

165
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,933
I heard Mr. Chan died
in that ambush,

166
00:07:46,067 --> 00:07:48,567
along with some NCIA agents?

167
00:07:48,733 --> 00:07:49,767
<i> You're right.</i>

168
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,167
Is that the case Dad
wanted you to drop?

169
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,200
Yes.

170
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:56,533
<i>It's a good thing
you're suspended.</i>

171
00:07:56,667 --> 00:07:58,967
<i>Otherwise, you would've been
caught in the ambush, too.</i>

172
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:01,433
Just drop that case, okay?

173
00:08:01,567 --> 00:08:02,467
Come home.

174
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:05,333
Do you want to have
dinner first? My treat.

175
00:08:06,267 --> 00:08:07,933
Max, thanks. But...

176
00:08:08,067 --> 00:08:09,800
I can't come home yet.

177
00:08:09,933 --> 00:08:11,267
<i> Why?</i>

178
00:08:11,267 --> 00:08:12,933
<i> Aren't you suspended?</i>

179
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:15,900
Well, I can't just let
the criminals

180
00:08:16,033 --> 00:08:17,533
who did this go free.

181
00:08:17,667 --> 00:08:19,000
<i> There you go again, Sam.</i>

182
00:08:19,133 --> 00:08:20,500
<i> You're not listening.</i>

183
00:08:20,633 --> 00:08:23,233
When will you choose to be
a good daughter to Dad

184
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:26,567
instead of being
a model agent at the NCIA?

185
00:08:27,267 --> 00:08:28,200
Hold on.

186
00:08:28,333 --> 00:08:30,767
I also need to clear my name.

187
00:08:30,767 --> 00:08:31,833
<i> Your name?</i>

188
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:33,367
<i> That's such a shallow excuse.</i>

189
00:08:33,367 --> 00:08:35,867
<i> You're so selfish, Sam.</i>

190
00:08:35,867 --> 00:08:38,167
You're only thinking
about yourself again.

191
00:08:38,167 --> 00:08:40,267
<i>Do you really not care
about Daddy anymore?</i>

192
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,800
Is that why you're disobeying
his orders?

193
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:45,133
<i>Max, we're both
in law enforcement.</i>

194
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:46,600
Is that what you do at the NLEA?

195
00:08:46,933 --> 00:08:49,100
When things get difficult,
you just drop the case?

196
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:52,100
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

197
00:08:52,233 --> 00:08:53,233
[SIGHS]

198
00:08:54,467 --> 00:08:55,033
Max, I'm sorry.

199
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,400
You know what?

200
00:08:58,867 --> 00:09:00,400
We don't have to talk anymore.

201
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,867
<i>You don't even have
to come home.</i>

202
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,300
<i>After all, you don't care
about us.</i>

203
00:09:04,433 --> 00:09:06,500
<i>So we don't care
about you either.</i>

204
00:09:07,533 --> 00:09:08,733
Max, Max...

205
00:09:18,967 --> 00:09:25,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

206
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:29,867
So, are we just going to
let Ma'am Sam leave?

207
00:09:30,467 --> 00:09:32,267
I'll handle it.
Stay right here.

208
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:38,933
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

209
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,067
Sam?

210
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:49,967
I'm sorry you had to hear that.

211
00:09:50,833 --> 00:09:53,000
We understand you.

212
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,333
It's a good thing
you understand me.

213
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:59,700
My family doesn't
understand me at all.

214
00:09:59,967 --> 00:10:02,133
We're all in law enforcement.

215
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:04,067
We all took the same oath,
just like the NLEA.

216
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:07,767
If anyone should understand me,
it should be them.

217
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:10,633
Maybe they're not speaking
as law enforcement officers...

218
00:10:10,767 --> 00:10:13,000
but as your family.

219
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,633
They're thinking about
what's best for you

220
00:10:15,967 --> 00:10:17,567
and your safety.

221
00:10:18,767 --> 00:10:19,833
No.

222
00:10:19,967 --> 00:10:21,433
That's not how I feel.

223
00:10:23,833 --> 00:10:25,333
I feel like...

224
00:10:26,633 --> 00:10:27,933
I feel like everything I do...

225
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:30,300
Every decision I make,
is wrong to them.

226
00:10:33,033 --> 00:10:34,867
Maybe it's because
they still haven't forgiven me

227
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:36,267
for what I did to them.

228
00:10:37,533 --> 00:10:39,533
Maybe you're the only one
thinking that,

229
00:10:39,667 --> 00:10:42,633
because you still
haven't forgiven yourself.

230
00:10:43,667 --> 00:10:50,400
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

231
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:54,200
Oh, Rudy.

232
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:57,467
What happened?
What did Betchay say?

233
00:10:57,467 --> 00:11:00,333
She's convincing me to settle.

234
00:11:00,967 --> 00:11:04,167
[ELTON] Well, what's new?

235
00:11:04,167 --> 00:11:07,867
When it comes to money,
you know Betchay's number one.

236
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:11,600
There's nothing wrong if you
accept their offer, Mister Rudy.

237
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,300
You're already doing fine,
after all.

238
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:15,933
Besides, I'm sure
that's big money.

239
00:11:15,933 --> 00:11:19,333
That is if Gabo accepts.

240
00:11:19,333 --> 00:11:22,833
But I think he'd prefer it
if the person who did that

241
00:11:22,833 --> 00:11:24,667
is held accountable.

242
00:11:26,333 --> 00:11:29,000
You know...

243
00:11:30,033 --> 00:11:31,833
Betchay has a point.

244
00:11:31,833 --> 00:11:33,833
We're not guaranteed
to win the case.

245
00:11:33,833 --> 00:11:37,367
But if I accept their money...

246
00:11:38,033 --> 00:11:40,300
We can use it to expand
the repair shop.

247
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:45,167
Or maybe to start
a new business.

248
00:11:45,167 --> 00:11:46,933
[ELTON] You do have
a point, Rudy.

249
00:11:46,933 --> 00:11:50,533
But I think you should
first talk with Gabo.

250
00:11:50,533 --> 00:11:51,833
You know how he is.

251
00:12:00,767 --> 00:12:02,067
Our problem's done!

252
00:12:03,367 --> 00:12:04,333
[DEBORAH] He's dead?

253
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:06,433
Not just Mr. Chan.

254
00:12:07,167 --> 00:12:10,100
But also the NCIA agents
who escorted him.

255
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:12,667
We included them,
so there'd be no witnesses.

256
00:12:12,667 --> 00:12:13,767
Good!

257
00:12:13,767 --> 00:12:16,833
Everything is going
according to plan.

258
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,800
Mr. Chan is dead.

259
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,300
They can't pin it all on Victor

260
00:12:22,300 --> 00:12:23,800
because their only witness
is dead.

261
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:28,500
But our next step should be
to get him out of jail.

262
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:34,200
Each day he's in jail,
our business gets affected.

263
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:36,567
This is all the fault
of that Agent Jacinto.

264
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:40,000
I won't stop
until I get my revenge.

265
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:43,533
My part's done, Lucas.

266
00:12:43,533 --> 00:12:44,767
It's your turn now.

267
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:47,967
Prove that you're not all bark.

268
00:12:48,833 --> 00:12:49,900
Yes, Pa.

269
00:12:51,167 --> 00:12:55,167
Lucas, you need to plan this
very carefully.

270
00:12:55,867 --> 00:12:58,367
You can't just charge forward
without thinking.

271
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:03,967
Wait for your target
to be alone and vulnerable.

272
00:13:03,967 --> 00:13:05,700
That's when you strike.

273
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:08,000
We'll ambush her tonight

274
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,433
when she's alone
on her way home.

275
00:13:12,967 --> 00:13:15,900
And when I'm certain
she's completely powerless.

276
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:22,367
[KAREN] Want us to eat first?
Your stomach shouldn't be empty.

277
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:25,467
- And don't be too sad.
- Yes.

278
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:28,200
[WOMAN CRYING]

279
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,400
Miss...

280
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:34,000
Where can I ask about
what happened in the ambush?

281
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,933
- What's your name, ma'am?
- Geraldine Damaso.

282
00:13:36,933 --> 00:13:38,467
[AGENT] I'll look for it.

283
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,467
[SAM] Uh, miss, excuse me.

284
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,800
Did I hear right?
Geraldine Damaso?

285
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:51,700
Yes.

286
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:55,533
Um, I am Agent Samantha Jacinto.

287
00:13:55,567 --> 00:13:58,100
Is Agent Erwin Damaso
your brother?

288
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:59,567
Yes.

289
00:13:59,567 --> 00:14:02,467
He's my older brother,
Erwin Damaso.

290
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:06,100
I just want to know
what happened to him.

291
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:09,067
Did anyone of them survive?
How did he die?

292
00:14:09,067 --> 00:14:11,567
[GERALDINE CRYING]

293
00:14:11,567 --> 00:14:13,067
You should take a seat.

294
00:14:13,067 --> 00:14:19,967
[GERALDINE CRYING, WHIMPERING]

295
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,600
Um...

296
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:29,267
Your brother was part
of the convoy.

297
00:14:31,033 --> 00:14:34,333
- Armed men ambushed them.
- My God...

298
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:35,467
[GERALDINE WHIMPERS]

299
00:14:37,700 --> 00:14:39,500
I don't know how--

300
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:41,800
how I'll tell my mom about this.

301
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,700
[GERALDINE CRYING]

302
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:46,100
My brother and I are
the only ones in Manila.

303
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:50,100
Our family's in the province.
I don't know what to do.

304
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:54,233
[GERALDINE CRYING]

305
00:14:54,233 --> 00:14:55,800
Geraldine, you have
to be strong.

306
00:15:01,967 --> 00:15:03,533
Who did this?

307
00:15:04,567 --> 00:15:05,967
Who?

308
00:15:05,967 --> 00:15:09,167
I know it won't bring back
my brother,

309
00:15:09,167 --> 00:15:11,633
but I hope you bring justice
for his death.

310
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,333
[GERALDINE SNIFFLES]

311
00:15:17,967 --> 00:15:19,867
My brother, God.

312
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:25,600
Geraldine, we promise
we'll do everything.

313
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:28,233
I will investigate
your brother's case myself.

314
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:31,067
We will catch
and hold accountable

315
00:15:31,067 --> 00:15:32,867
the people who killed him.

316
00:15:32,867 --> 00:15:37,500
[GERALDINE CRYING]

317
00:15:37,533 --> 00:15:38,600
Thank you.

318
00:15:40,933 --> 00:15:47,967
[GERALDINE CRYING]

319
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:56,233
Alright, Gabo.
Pick what you want to use.

320
00:15:57,667 --> 00:16:01,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

321
00:16:01,133 --> 00:16:05,200
[GUNS COCK]

322
00:16:06,867 --> 00:16:10,733
[TOMAS] Semi-automatic.
Oliver frame, light.

323
00:16:10,767 --> 00:16:12,567
But it doesn't look like
a toy.

324
00:16:12,567 --> 00:16:15,467
- [OMENG] Black finish!
- [TOMAS] Polymer grip.

325
00:16:15,467 --> 00:16:17,900
Textured to avoid slipping.

326
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:19,367
If the first one's
for face-to-face fights,

327
00:16:19,367 --> 00:16:20,667
this one's more versatile.

328
00:16:20,667 --> 00:16:27,633
[GUNSHOTS]

329
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:32,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

330
00:16:32,567 --> 00:16:33,700
[GUNSHOT]

331
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:36,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

332
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,233
[GUNSHOT]

333
00:16:38,167 --> 00:16:40,300
[LAWIN] For something
ala competition-style...

334
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:43,167
It's long, makes clean
but aggressive shots.

335
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:45,433
[TOMAS] The bullets
are different.

336
00:16:45,433 --> 00:16:49,367
Some are laced with poison.
Others, blow up when fired.

337
00:16:50,333 --> 00:16:54,533
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

338
00:16:54,533 --> 00:16:55,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

339
00:16:55,733 --> 00:16:56,833
[GUNSHOT]

340
00:16:56,833 --> 00:16:59,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

341
00:17:01,967 --> 00:17:03,733
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

342
00:17:03,733 --> 00:17:05,533
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

343
00:17:05,533 --> 00:17:10,733
[GUNSHOTS]

344
00:17:10,733 --> 00:17:14,833
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

345
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:18,167
[GUNSHOTS]

346
00:17:19,167 --> 00:17:21,367
[ENGINE REVVING]

347
00:17:21,367 --> 00:17:26,067
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

348
00:17:26,067 --> 00:17:28,967
[GUNSHOTS]

349
00:17:28,967 --> 00:17:30,667
[ENGINE REVVING]

350
00:17:30,667 --> 00:17:33,100
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [ENGINE REVVING]

351
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:36,600
[GUNSHOTS]

352
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:40,100
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

353
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,467
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

354
00:17:41,467 --> 00:17:45,467
[GUNSHOTS]

355
00:17:45,467 --> 00:17:47,533
[TOMAS] Now that
you're holding the gun...

356
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:50,133
You must remember
your responsibility.

357
00:17:50,133 --> 00:17:52,967
You must only fire
at your enemies.

358
00:17:52,967 --> 00:17:55,400
[PAPANG] That gun
is a friend.

359
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:59,233
But it can also be
a hostile enemy.

360
00:17:59,233 --> 00:18:03,833
It's up to you to decide
if it'll be your friend or not.

361
00:18:05,433 --> 00:18:07,767
I've avoided holding a gun
for a long time.

362
00:18:09,167 --> 00:18:10,933
But I promise you.

363
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:14,633
I'll use this
for the greater good.

364
00:18:15,833 --> 00:18:22,800
[HEROIC MUSIC PLAYING]

365
00:18:34,433 --> 00:18:35,700
- [ISOBEL CLEARS THROAT]
- Pinky was here?

366
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:36,933
What did she want?

367
00:18:38,267 --> 00:18:40,400
She was just checking in.

368
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:41,967
To see how Sam is doing.

369
00:18:41,967 --> 00:18:45,700
I also apologized
for your behavior last night.

370
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:51,667
Do you share our
family's problems with others?

371
00:18:51,667 --> 00:18:52,733
Why?

372
00:18:53,367 --> 00:18:54,867
What's your problem?

373
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:57,600
Pinky is a family friend.

374
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,233
And don't forget

375
00:18:59,233 --> 00:19:03,200
who made a scene last night
in front of the guests

376
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:05,567
and humiliated
his own daughter.

377
00:19:05,567 --> 00:19:07,700
Because she has
brought shame to this family.

378
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:10,633
She's the first Jacinto to be
suspended by the agency.

379
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:14,200
She's lucky
I didn't kick her out.

380
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:16,167
What difference will it make?

381
00:19:16,167 --> 00:19:19,367
You treat her horribly.

382
00:19:19,367 --> 00:19:22,200
It's like you're not
even family!

383
00:19:23,767 --> 00:19:26,200
Like she's not your daughter!

384
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:33,200
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

385
00:19:41,433 --> 00:19:48,433
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

386
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:55,400
Ma'am Sam.

387
00:19:57,167 --> 00:19:59,133
I think you should go home.

388
00:19:59,133 --> 00:20:01,033
Get some rest.

389
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:02,700
Any leads on
this motorcycle?

390
00:20:02,733 --> 00:20:04,867
We know it belongs to
the man we encountered

391
00:20:04,867 --> 00:20:06,633
when we caught Tiger.

392
00:20:06,633 --> 00:20:08,933
Are you talking about
the guy with the long hair?

393
00:20:08,933 --> 00:20:10,800
Zafra mentioned him to me.

394
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:13,200
I think he's the key
to all of this.

395
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:14,467
Ma'am.

396
00:20:14,467 --> 00:20:17,233
Where and how
are you going to find him?

397
00:20:17,233 --> 00:20:19,300
With all due respect, Sam,

398
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:20,600
I don't think
this is going to work.

399
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:23,667
We have no leads.
It's like chasing a dead end.

400
00:20:23,667 --> 00:20:25,733
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

401
00:20:27,133 --> 00:20:29,700
I think I should drop this case.

402
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:32,267
I just can't solve it.

403
00:20:32,267 --> 00:20:34,000
I'm not a good agent.

404
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,733
Sam, this is stress talking.

405
00:20:36,767 --> 00:20:38,633
You just need
to take a break.

406
00:20:38,633 --> 00:20:42,300
You know,
just step away for a while.

407
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:43,433
She's right, Ma'am Sam.

408
00:20:43,433 --> 00:20:44,900
We'll take over
while you're gone.

409
00:20:44,900 --> 00:20:46,133
I'll go to the site.

410
00:20:46,133 --> 00:20:48,767
I'll gather intel
about the ambush.

411
00:20:48,767 --> 00:20:49,800
Don't worry.

412
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,467
We'll solve this case.

413
00:20:51,467 --> 00:20:52,967
I'll go on ahead, team.

414
00:20:52,967 --> 00:20:54,733
- Bye.
- Be careful.

415
00:20:56,067 --> 00:20:57,467
Get some rest.

416
00:20:59,533 --> 00:21:06,533
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

417
00:21:08,767 --> 00:21:13,667
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

418
00:21:13,667 --> 00:21:17,033
It's not your equipment
or your weapons, Gabo...

419
00:21:17,033 --> 00:21:21,367
Your mind is
your greatest asset.

420
00:21:22,667 --> 00:21:27,933
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

421
00:21:27,933 --> 00:21:30,667
Sometimes,
there are things invisible

422
00:21:30,667 --> 00:21:32,767
to the naked eye,

423
00:21:32,767 --> 00:21:35,467
but the people around you
can see them.

424
00:21:35,467 --> 00:21:37,800
So you have to
move quickly.

425
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,700
Before they make a move.

426
00:21:41,333 --> 00:21:46,000
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

427
00:21:46,033 --> 00:21:49,033
Don't be so aggressive.

428
00:21:49,033 --> 00:21:51,300
Patience is a virtue.

429
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:55,267
You have to analyze
every move you make.

430
00:21:56,767 --> 00:21:59,933
[TOMAS]
Open your mind, Gabo.

431
00:21:59,933 --> 00:22:03,033
Then you'll come up
with the right strategy

432
00:22:03,033 --> 00:22:05,433
and plan your attack.

433
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:10,333
[PAPANG]
Before the fight even begins,

434
00:22:10,333 --> 00:22:14,367
you need to be sure
you'll win.

435
00:22:14,367 --> 00:22:19,167
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

436
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:20,933
In a person's life,

437
00:22:22,867 --> 00:22:24,967
sometimes you need speed...

438
00:22:26,367 --> 00:22:29,400
so you can move undetected.

439
00:22:29,400 --> 00:22:31,400
I was born in Tondo,

440
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:33,267
in Ginintuang Lupa.

441
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:39,333
So I know how the
people there live and think.

442
00:22:39,333 --> 00:22:40,967
With every move I make...

443
00:22:40,967 --> 00:22:43,333
my opponent doesn't realize

444
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:46,067
I've already beaten them.

445
00:22:48,333 --> 00:22:49,433
Checkmate.

446
00:22:49,467 --> 00:22:52,600
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

447
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:54,067
[LAWIN] He got lucky.

448
00:22:54,067 --> 00:22:55,333
He distracted you.

449
00:22:58,733 --> 00:23:01,200
That wasn't luck.

450
00:23:03,033 --> 00:23:06,733
Gabo, you are
a remarkable man.

451
00:23:06,733 --> 00:23:12,200
Your intelligence goes far
beyond what school can teach.

452
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:17,433
You earned your wisdom
through your own experiences.

453
00:23:17,433 --> 00:23:21,067
Keep going, Gabo.

454
00:23:21,067 --> 00:23:24,200
That will be your greatest asset
in this mission.

455
00:23:24,233 --> 00:23:28,067
[STIRRING MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

456
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:32,867
Uh, Pops, I'll head out now.

457
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,800
Okay.

458
00:23:34,933 --> 00:23:36,267
Be careful, Gabo.

459
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:38,900
We'll call you

460
00:23:39,033 --> 00:23:41,600
when it's almost time
for the next mission.

461
00:23:45,700 --> 00:23:48,533
Pops, I'm sorry.

462
00:23:49,233 --> 00:23:52,200
I know what I'm about
to do is wrong, but...

463
00:23:53,833 --> 00:23:55,733
if it's possible, maybe...

464
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:57,067
...could I borrow some money?

465
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:59,000
Even just
a hundred thousand pesos.

466
00:23:59,133 --> 00:24:01,300
I really have something
I need it for.

467
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:02,567
[SCOFFS]

468
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:05,633
You're something
else, Gabo, huh?

469
00:24:06,733 --> 00:24:08,167
The mission hasn't even started,

470
00:24:08,300 --> 00:24:09,600
and you're already asking
for money.

471
00:24:09,733 --> 00:24:11,467
You haven't even done
anything,

472
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:13,167
and you're already asking
to get paid?

473
00:24:15,700 --> 00:24:17,567
Earlier, on my way here,

474
00:24:19,133 --> 00:24:21,600
I helped a mother and child
who'd been robbed.

475
00:24:22,367 --> 00:24:24,133
I took the mother
to the hospital.

476
00:24:24,267 --> 00:24:25,933
I felt bad for the kid.

477
00:24:26,900 --> 00:24:30,100
And I don't want the child
to go through what I...

478
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:32,467
...went through when
my mother died.

479
00:24:32,600 --> 00:24:33,533
That's why I want to help them.

480
00:24:35,267 --> 00:24:36,600
That's your strength, Gabo.

481
00:24:38,633 --> 00:24:40,100
Your heart.

482
00:24:42,733 --> 00:24:45,033
[OMENG]
That's your strength, Gabo.

483
00:24:45,167 --> 00:24:47,000
But it'll also be your weakness.

484
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:49,800
And your enemies
will use that against you.

485
00:24:51,133 --> 00:24:55,500
But Gabo's heart
is in the right place, Omeng.

486
00:24:56,200 --> 00:24:58,767
Because no one
will help a fellow Filipino

487
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:00,767
if we don't help each other.

488
00:25:02,433 --> 00:25:10,200
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

489
00:25:17,367 --> 00:25:18,667
Pops...

490
00:25:19,433 --> 00:25:21,500
Thank you so, so much
for your help.

491
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:22,733
Don't worry.

492
00:25:22,867 --> 00:25:25,100
I'll really give this
to the mother and child

493
00:25:25,233 --> 00:25:27,000
so I can help them.

494
00:25:27,133 --> 00:25:28,200
Okay, Gabo.

495
00:25:28,333 --> 00:25:30,667
Help them.

496
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:34,100
Take care of whatever
needs to be taken care of.

497
00:25:34,233 --> 00:25:36,600
Yes, Pops.

498
00:25:36,767 --> 00:25:38,767
I'll head out now.
Thank you again.

499
00:25:44,333 --> 00:25:51,300
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

500
00:25:56,133 --> 00:25:57,500
<i>It's so dead!
There's no customers!</i>

501
00:25:57,500 --> 00:25:58,767
<i> I'm here!</i>

502
00:25:58,900 --> 00:26:00,933
<i>You're the one
who brings the energy</i>

503
00:26:01,067 --> 00:26:02,967
<i> and the money to BeerGin.</i>

504
00:26:03,100 --> 00:26:05,600
<i>Why don't you just
manage this?</i>

505
00:26:05,733 --> 00:26:07,533
<i> She's just a nobody.</i>

506
00:26:07,667 --> 00:26:09,533
[GUNSHOTS]

507
00:26:09,700 --> 00:26:11,167
<i> It should be an easy job.</i>

508
00:26:12,033 --> 00:26:14,400
<i> Sam's at Soriano Street.</i>

509
00:26:14,833 --> 00:26:15,900
[GUNSHOTS]

510
